TimeCheck: Let audio calls go on after a timeout

With the abort on a timeout commented out, the expired request stayed
first in line. Every pass of the loop timed out on it again, asked for
HAL tombstones and slept a second, all while holding the lock every
audio binder call takes to start and stop its own TimeCheck. One audio
HAL call over 5 seconds, such as the Echo Dot's HAL starting at boot,
froze audioserver until it restarted.

Drop the request once it has timed out and wait for the tombstones
outside the lock.

diff --git a/media/utils/TimeCheck.cpp b/media/utils/TimeCheck.cpp
index 46a4ec8..ca38284 100644
--- a/media/utils/TimeCheck.cpp
+++ b/media/utils/TimeCheck.cpp
@@ -99,6 +99,7 @@ void TimeCheck::TimeCheckThread::stopMonitoring(nsecs_t endTimeNs) {
 bool TimeCheck::TimeCheckThread::threadLoop()
 {
     status_t status = TIMED_OUT;
+    bool waitForTombstones = false;
     {
         AutoMutex _l(mMutex);
 
@@ -119,6 +120,14 @@ bool TimeCheck::TimeCheckThread::threadLoop()
             status = mCond.waitRelative(mMutex, waitTimeNs);
         }
         if (status != NO_ERROR) {
+            // Without the abort below, the expired request has to go: left in
+            // place it timed out again on every pass, and the loop held the
+            // lock every audio binder call takes, so one slow call froze
+            // audioserver for good. The call's own TimeCheck finds nothing to
+            // remove when it ends.
+            if (mMonitorRequests.size() != 0 && mMonitorRequests.keyAt(0) == endTimeNs) {
+                mMonitorRequests.removeItemsAt(0);
+            }
             // Generate audio HAL processes tombstones and allow time to complete
             // before forcing restart
             std::vector<pid_t> pids = getAudioHalPids();
@@ -127,7 +136,7 @@ bool TimeCheck::TimeCheckThread::threadLoop()
                     ALOGI("requesting tombstone for pid: %d", pid);
                     sigqueue(pid, DEBUGGER_SIGNAL, {.sival_int = 0});
                 }
-                sleep(1);
+                waitForTombstones = true;
             } else {
                 ALOGI("No HAL process pid available, skipping tombstones");
             }
@@ -135,6 +144,8 @@ bool TimeCheck::TimeCheckThread::threadLoop()
             // LOG_ALWAYS_FATAL("TimeCheck timeout for %s", tag);
         }
     }
+    // Outside the lock, so the audio calls go on meanwhile.
+    if (waitForTombstones) sleep(1);
     return true;
 }
 
